{title: Nothing but Joy}
{subtitle: James 1:2–3}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [Bbmaj7] | [Ebsus2] | [Bbmaj7] | [Ebsus2] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Consider it nothing [F/A]but joy, my brothers
[Gm]Whenever we fall in[F/A]to trials of every [Eb]kind
You know the test[Bb/D]ing of your faith
[Cm7]Produces endu[Fsus4]rance in our daily [Bb]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Nothing but [Bb]joy, nothing but [F/A]joy
Even when [Gm7]the trials come to find [Eb]us
Nothing but [Bb]joy, nothing but [F/A]joy
Endurance [Gm7]grows and our spirits bind [Eb]us
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Let en[Bb]durance finish its [F/A]holy work
So that [Gm7]we may be mature [Eb]and complete
[Bb]Lacking nothing in this [F/A]sacred path
Where our [Gm7]faith is tested and [Eb]made sweet
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Nothing but [Bb]joy, nothing but [F/A]joy
Even when the [Gm7]trials come to find [Eb]us
Nothing but [Bb]joy, nothing but [F/A]joy
Endurance [Gm7]grows and our spirits bind [Eb]us
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
If [Gm]any of you lacks [F/A]wisdom, ask God
He gives [Bb]generously to all [Eb]without fault
[Gm]Ask in faith, without [F/A]doubting or fear
Like a [Eb]wave, do not let the wind halt [F]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Ma[Gm]ture and com[Bbmaj7]plete, lacking [Eb]nothing
Nothing but [Gm]joy, nothing but [F][Eb]joy
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
